    description: "Invariant: a symbol carrying meta.framework_role=route (route_framework set) is classified as an http_route entrypoint and appears in the sketch's \"HTTP Routes\" section.\n\nViolated on thc (pristine clone @ 0ab75985d, hypergumbo 8.1.0 @ ea165f53fa, 2026-10-06): lib/thunderhillcinema_web/router.ex yields 377 function symbols named like \"GET /users/csrf_refresh\" with meta {framework_role: route, route_framework: phoenix, http_method, route_path, controller, action} and 373 dispatches_to edges -- but entrypoints holds 436 library_export and only 2 http_route (both scanner/server.js, Express). The router symbols carry concepts=[library_export]. The sketch's HTTP Routes section lists only the Express /scan and /health; router.ex has ~339 get/post/live/... lines. Check analogues: other route frameworks whose route symbols are kind=function."  # c7d9
    fields:  # c7d9
      statement: "A symbol carrying meta.framework_role=route (route_framework set) is classified as an http_route entrypoint and appears in the sketch's HTTP Routes section."  # c7d9
      root_cause: "Not yet investigated. Observed: the Phoenix router symbols are kind=function with concepts=[library_export]; the entrypoint classifier appears to take the library_export concept over the route meta."  # c7d9
